:"I'm looking at a twin prisoner's dilemma where the two copies receive different inputs. Under the A-FDT view, both copies run the same function, and the input differences in names and lead text don't matter. The essay treats the correlation as near one when no relevant difference exists, so cooperating yields the better outcome of 2 versus 4. I'll choose to pass.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9715,"completion_tokens":512,"total_tokens":10227,"cost":0.0491,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.0491,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.03886,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01024},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":96,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}